  "lastName": "Gibbs",
  "overview": "Dr. Victoria (Katie) Gibbs completed her graduate research training in aquatic animal nutritional physiology and her post-graduate training in pre-clinical aging biology, focusing on energetics and individual variation in lifespan. Her research work with aquatic invertebrates and murine models gives her a unique perspective to share with students in the Biomedical Science Program (BMD), how basic biology and applied sciences interact to benefit society. Dr. Gibbs gained valuable instructional and mentoring skills during her tenure teaching in a liberal arts environment, and she applies those skills in her physiology courses in BMD.",
